│  # Model Card — Customer Churn                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  ## Model details                                                            │
│                                                                              │
│  - Model task: binary churn prediction for customer retention outreach       │
│  - Selected model: random_forest                                             │
│  - Selection rule: highest 5-fold cross-validated ROC-AUC on the training    │
│  set                                                                         │
│  - Decision threshold: 0.5                                                   │
│  - Contract version: 1.0                                                     │
│  - Random seed: 42                                                           │
│  - Total features: 26                                                        │
│  - Training rows: 4059                                                       │
│  - Test rows: 1015                                                           │
│  - Training churn rate: 16.6%                                                │
│  - Test churn rate: 16.6%                                                    │
│                                                                              │
│  The model uses customer activity, satisfaction, order, and payment-related  │
│  features. Gender and MaritalStatus were excluded from the feature set.      │
│                                                                              │
│  ## Intended use                                                             │
│                                                                              │
│  This model is intended to rank customers for retention outreach.            │
│                                                                              │
│  Appropriate uses:                                                           │
│  - Prioritizing customers for outreach, offers, or intervention              │
│  - Ranking customers by churn risk for operational follow-up                 │
│  - Supporting retention campaign planning                                    │
│                                                                              │
│  Out-of-scope uses:                                                          │
│  - Hiring, lending, insurance, housing, or other decisions unrelated to      │
│  retention                                                                   │
│  - Any use as a sole basis for automated adverse action                      │
│  - Any use that treats the score as a causal explanation of churn            │
│  - Any use outside the dataset contract and feature engineering pipeline     │
│                                                                              │
│  ## Training data                                                            │
│                                                                              │
│  The model was trained under contract version 1.0.                           │
│                                                                              │
│  Contract assumptions:                                                       │
│  - One row per customer; CustomerID is unique.                               │
│  - Churn is the target: 1 = customer churned, 0 = customer stayed.           │
│  - Missing numeric values were filled with the median of the respective      │
│  column.                                                                     │
│  - 556 duplicate rows were removed during cleaning.                          │
│  - Inconsistent category spellings were merged: Phone was changed to Mobile  │
│  Phone, CC was changed to Credit Card, and COD was changed to Cash on        │
│  Delivery.                                                                   │
│                                                                              │
│  Feature set:                                                                │
│  - Numeric columns used: Tenure, CityTier, WarehouseToHome, HourSpendOnApp,  │
│  NumberOfDeviceRegistered, SatisfactionScore, NumberOfAddress, Complain,     │
│  OrderAmountHikeFromlastYear, CouponUsed, OrderCount, DaySinceLastOrder,     │
│  CashbackAmount                                                              │
│  - One-hot encoded text columns: PreferredLoginDevice,                       │
│  PreferredPaymentMode, PreferedOrderCat                                      │
│  - Engineered features:                                                      │
│    - is_new_customer: 1 if Tenure <= 1 month                                 │
│    - cashback_per_order: CashbackAmount / OrderCount, with OrderCount        │
│  floored at 1                                                                │
│    - coupons_per_order: CouponUsed / OrderCount, with OrderCount floored at  │
│  1                                                                           │
│    - days_since_order_per_tenure: DaySinceLastOrder / (Tenure + 1)           │
│                                                                              │
│  Validation passed with 71 contract checks and 0 violations.                 │
│                                                                              │
│  ## Evaluation                                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  The selected model is random_forest because it had the highest 5-fold       │
│  cross-validated ROC-AUC on the training set.                                │
│                                                                              │
│  Model comparison on the held-out test set:                                  │
│                                                                              │
│  - logistic_regression                                                       │
│    - CV ROC-AUC: 89.4% ± 1.5%                                                │
│    - ROC-AUC: 89.0%                                                          │
│    - PR-AUC: 68.3%                                                           │
│    - Precision: 47.8%                                                        │
│    - Recall: 83.3%                                                           │
│    - F1: 60.7%                                                               │
│  - random_forest                                                             │
│    - CV ROC-AUC: 96.0% ± 0.7%                                                │
│    - ROC-AUC: 98.0%                                                          │
│    - PR-AUC: 92.6%                                                           │
│    - Precision: 75.9%                                                        │
│    - Recall: 91.7%                                                           │
│    - F1: 83.0%                                                               │
│  - gradient_boosting                                                         │
│    - CV ROC-AUC: 95.9% ± 1.2%                                                │
│    - ROC-AUC: 98.5%                                                          │
│    - PR-AUC: 95.2%                                                           │
│    - Precision: 80.9%                                                        │
│    - Recall: 93.5%                                                           │
│    - F1: 86.7%                                                               │
│                                                                              │
│  Top permutation importance features:                                        │
│  - Complain: 4.5%                                                            │
│  - Tenure: 2.6%                                                              │
│  - NumberOfAddress: 2.5%                                                     │
│  - is_new_customer: 1.8%                                                     │
│  - SatisfactionScore: 1.5%                                                   │
│  - CashbackAmount: 1.3%                                                      │
│  - cashback_per_order: 1.1%                                                  │
│  - CityTier: 1.0%                                                            │
│  - days_since_order_per_tenure: 1.0%                                         │
│  - WarehouseToHome: 1.0%                                                     │
│                                                                              │
│  Important note: importance does not show direction. A feature with high     │
│  importance may matter a lot to the model, but this does not tell us         │
│  whether higher values increase or decrease churn risk.                      │
│                                                                              │
│  ## Limitations                                                              │
│                                                                              │
│  There is mild leakage in the preprocessing pipeline: Crew 1 filled missing  │
│  numeric values with medians computed on the full dataset before the         │
│  train/test split. That means the test distribution influenced               │
│  preprocessing. This is a mild leak, not a catastrophic one, but it can      │
│  make reported performance slightly optimistic.                              │
│                                                                              │
│  Other limitations:                                                          │
│  - The model is evaluated on one fixed train/test split; results may vary    │
│  on new data.                                                                │
│  - Very strong test metrics may not fully transfer to production data.       │
│  - Permutation importance does not tell us the direction of effects.         │
│  - The model can only learn patterns present in the training data and the    │
│  contract-defined features.                                                  │
│  - Excluding sensitive columns does not guarantee fairness.                  │
│                                                                              │
│  ## Ethical considerations                                                   │
│                                                                              │
│  Gender and MaritalStatus were excluded from the features. That reduces      │
│  direct use of those columns, but it does not guarantee fairness.            │
│                                                                              │
│  Fairness by group, reported as actual churn rate, flagged rate, and         │
│  recall:                                                                     │
│                                                                              │
│  Gender:                                                                     │
│  - Female                                                                    │
│    - Customers: 404                                                          │
│    - Actual churn rate: 18.6%                                                │
│    - Flagged rate: 22.8%                                                     │
│    - Recall: 85.3%                                                           │
│  - Male                                                                      │
│    - Customers: 611                                                          │
│    - Actual churn rate: 15.2%                                                │
